  "notes": "USAGE:\nA versatile word used across many domains. In medicine, it means pain relief or palliative care ({緩和|かんわ}ケア). In economics and politics, {規制|きせい}{緩和|かんわ} (deregulation) and {金融|きんゆう}{緩和|かんわ} (monetary easing) are key terms. In diplomacy, it describes easing of tensions.\n\nWATCH OUT:\nNot to be confused with {漢和|かんわ} (Chinese-Japanese, as in {漢和|かんわ}{辞典|じてん}, a kanji dictionary).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {規制|きせい}{緩和|かんわ}: deregulation, relaxation of regulations\n- {金融|きんゆう}{緩和|かんわ}: monetary easing\n- {緊張|きんちょう}{緩和|かんわ}: easing of tensions, détente\n- {緩和|かんわ}ケア: palliative care\n- {痛|いた}みの{緩和|かんわ}: pain relief",
